Australian Product Guide — Consumer experience / authority depth v14 current release record
Release date: 2026-08-17
Production source: GitHub main via Vercel
Canonical production domain: https://australianproductguide.au

Current platform: authority depth v14 over semantic Scout/readability v13, illustrative consumer experience v12, institutional v9 consumer design, v11 footer/navigation, Decision Lab, My APG local-first workspace with optional account sync, universal search, comparison, buying guides, trust surfaces, responsive accessibility hardening and privacy-first analytics consent. Architecture remains lightweight SSR-first Node with progressive enhancement.

Catalogue truth: 471 maintained products; 90 populated categories; 176 represented brands. National high-intent categories remain manufacturer-backed, with televisions and laptops deepened to seven maintained models each. Coffee grinders, home printers and pizza ovens are promoted through authority-depth v14 with exact Australian manufacturer specifications, documented trade-offs, related-decision pathways and separately verified retailer/support evidence. Starter evidence elsewhere remains explicitly labelled.

Consumer-readability truth: the homepage decision-panel label is now high-contrast navy text on APG gold, and supporting small text across the decision panel, coverage strip, situation cards, journey cards and trust surfaces has stronger contrast and line-height. The goal is readable consumer guidance rather than decorative low-contrast typography.

Shopping-assistant truth: APG now uses Scout, an original APG shopping-guide character. Scout accepts natural-language needs, preserves conversational context across refinements, calls the existing deterministic /api/decision engine, explains fit reasons and compromises, and hands shoppers to product evidence, Compare or Decision Lab. Scout does not introduce commercial recommendation weighting.

Semantic-visual truth: national product-card visuals for televisions, laptops, washing machines, fridges, dishwashers and smartphones replace the legacy generic headphone fallback in the browser with category-correct APG-authored SVGs. Exact third-party product photography remains rights-gated; APG does not scrape or fabricate product imagery.

Retailer and evidence truth: Amazon Australia currently has 23 independently verified exact product destinations; the other 448 maintained products use transparent model-specific Amazon search fallbacks rather than guessed ASINs. Select exact non-Amazon Australian retailer pathways are surfaced for verified LG C6, MacBook Air M5 and Bosch WGG244F0AU records, and authority categories expose verified Australian brand/retailer/support pathways. Retailer availability and commission contribute zero recommendation points. APG does not claim whole-of-market price comparison.

Independent-evidence truth: selected high-intent products surface attributed professional evidence separately from exact Australian manufacturer identity. Independent review evidence is never converted into a claim that APG performed hands-on testing, and family/size/configuration differences are disclosed where relevant.

Search and Decision Intelligence: national-category search relevance is tightened in the consumer layer so interpreted TV, laptop, washing-machine, fridge, dishwasher and smartphone queries suppress unrelated product-card noise in the rendered search experience. Scout and Decision Lab share the maintained zero-commercial-weight decision engine and expose reasons/trade-offs rather than opaque rankings.

Freshness control: a weekly GitHub Actions catalogue audit is installed. It checks duplicate/missing product identity, provenance/freshness fields, overdue review windows and exact-Amazon identifier/affiliate-tag integrity. The audit flags review debt and hard data defects; it does not auto-publish factual product changes.

Privacy/analytics: Google Analytics remains opt-in. Analytics storage defaults to denied and the GA script is loaded only after the visitor allows analytics. My APG remains local-first and usable without login; account status does not affect recommendations.

Release discipline: GitHub main is authoritative; Vercel Production must match the current source SHA; canonical public pages, changed assets, retailer/evidence surfaces, decision API behaviour, security/privacy controls and representative responsive journeys must be verified before closing the release. A representative Production verification is not represented as a fresh browser crawl of every canonical route.